WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit
2: Celebrations and Festivals.

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.360
In this unit you will explore celebrations
and festivals from around the world,

3
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.680
with a special focus on traditions that matter
to communities across East Africa and beyond.

4
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.080
Festivals bring people together.

5
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.600
They remind us of our history, our values,
and the things that make each culture unique.

6
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:29.080
Whether it is the joy of a national independence
day, the colourful lanterns of a harvest celebration,

7
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:34.460
or the excitement of a local sports
day, every festival has a story to tell.

8
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:40.260
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:47.000
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
understand texts about different festivals and celebrations.

10
00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:53.040
You will also use prepositions of time (in,
on, at) correctly in speech and writing.

11
00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:59.570
You will also recognise and form compound
adjectives (hand-made, brightly coloured).

12
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.040
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:11.700
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: allocation,
ambiguity, applicability, approximation, lyric, cooperative.

14
00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:17.880
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:22.160
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:30.620
The reading sequence includes Festivals That Bring Us
Together, part 1 and Festivals That Bring Us Together, part 2.

17
00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.220
Read actively.

18
00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:37.780
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:41.800
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:48.760
The first language focus is
Prepositions of Time: In, On and At.

21
00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:56.400
Prepositions of time tell your reader exactly when
something happens: in holds long stretches of time,

22
00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:01.120
on lands on particular days and dates,
and at points to precise moments.

23
00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:08.520
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.760
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Compare Two Festivals.

25
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.380
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.820
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.520
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.180
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:33.580
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.260
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:44.160
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
